## You need to link your new processor edn given by MPD Sir in this directory so that 
   bitgen.tcl in vivado_synth can access it for bitstream generation.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-Because processor_1x1x32.edn file was too large , it could not be uploaded in repo

-EDN files will be needed for bistream generation of VCU118 Aparajit in madhav system 
   (VLSI lab server having vivado license) so follow:-
   1. Make a directory named  " new_<date> " [useful for identifaction of latest edn].
   2. Upload  processor_1x1x32.edn inside this directory.


  NOTE : This repo is already git clonnned in madhav system (lab server) and latest edn files will be there.

